Article 14

1. The Regional Government is obliged and responsible to carry out efforts to protect women and children victims of violence through:
a. determination of policies;
b. preparation of program and activity planning;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
d. allocating a budget;
e. establishment of a Children's Forum; and
f. establishment of a Task Force.
2. To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government organizes services for victims in the form of:
a. facilitating the establishment of P2TP2A;
b. facilitating P2TP2A facilities and infrastructure according to the Region's capacity; and
c. facilitating the Task Force as a network forum for handling Victims.

Article 16

The community and family have obligations and responsibilities which include:
a. preventing the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. reporting if violence occurs;
c. protecting victims; and
d. providing emergency assistance.

Article 19

1. The organizational structure of P2TP2A established by the Regional Government as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (1) consists of:
a. chairperson or other equivalent designation;
b. 7 general vice chairpersons;
c. secretary;
d. treasurer;
e. executive chairperson; and
f. executive vice chairperson.
2. The establishment, structure, and duties of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) are determined by Regent's Decree.

Article 25

Forms of services to victims include:
a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. assistance services;
c. health services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services; and
f. repatriation and social reintegration services.
